      "writtenOn": "2022-08-16T05:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We use uint8_t here as this is used as a byte array and also the bluetooth::audio::sco::read/write and the underlying UIPC_Read/Write all use uint8_t. If we want to better reflect the data\u0027s actual format, we should probably use int16_t as the PCM for HFP should be S16_LE. However, changing this to int16_t without making changes on the sco::read/write interface makes less sense. I also think it\u0027s probably not worth it to add the format assumption here.",
      "parentUuid": "2f9ba5bb_a286ffd1",
