      "writtenOn": "2022-08-16T05:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "True.\n\nAs my reply for the hfp_msbc_encode_frames type question, I think we should still use uint8_t for bytes buffer here. But I do agree that it looks weird and not very safe to do the casting here. Thus, I\u0027ve changed the interface of hfp_msbc_encode_frames to digest the uint8_t bytes and do the casting there when passing the data buffer to the actual SBC encoder. It\u0027s clearer that the SBC encoder requires the input data to be int16_t format",
